#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:179
msgid "Recipe Maintenance Tracking Data Moved to OE-Core"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:181
msgid ""
"Maintenance tracking data for recipes that was previously part of ``meta-"
"yocto`` has been moved to :term:`OpenEmbedded-Core (OE-Core)`. The change"
" includes ``package_regex.inc`` and ``distro_alias.inc``, which are "
"typically enabled when using the ``distrodata`` class. Additionally, the "
"contents of ``upstream_tracking.inc`` has now been split out to the "
"relevant recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:191
msgid "Automatic Stale Sysroot File Cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:193
msgid ""
"Stale files from recipes that no longer exist in the current "
"configuration are now automatically removed from sysroot as well as "
"removed from any other place managed by shared state. This automatic "
"cleanup means that the build system now properly handles situations such "
"as renaming the build system side of recipes, removal of layers from :ref"
":`structure-build-conf-bblayers.conf`, and :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:201
msgid ""
"Additionally, work directories for old versions of recipes are now "
"pruned. If you wish to disable pruning old work directories, you can set "
"the following variable in your configuration::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:210
msgid "``linux-yocto`` Kernel Metadata Repository Now Split from Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:212
msgid ""
"The ``linux-yocto`` tree has up to now been a combined set of kernel "
"changes and configuration (meta) data carried in a single tree. While "
"this format is effective at keeping kernel configuration and source "
"modifications synchronized, it is not always obvious to developers how to"
" manipulate the Metadata as compared to the source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:218
msgid ""
"Metadata processing has now been removed from the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"kernel-yocto` class and the external Metadata repository ``yocto-kernel-"
"cache``, which has always been used to seed the ``linux-yocto`` \"meta\" "
"branch. This separate ``linux-yocto`` cache repository is now the primary"
" location for this data. Due to this change, ``linux-yocto`` is no longer"
" able to process combined trees. Thus, if you need to have your own "
"combined kernel repository, you must do the split there as well and "
"update your recipes accordingly. See the ``meta/recipes-kernel/linux"
"/linux-yocto_4.1.bb`` recipe for an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:231
msgid "Additional QA checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:233
msgid "The following QA checks have been added:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:235
msgid ""
"Added a \"host-user-contaminated\" check for ownership issues for "
"packaged files outside of ``/home``. The check looks for files that are "
"incorrectly owned by the user that ran BitBake instead of owned by a "
"valid user in the target system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:240
msgid ""
"Added an \"invalid-chars\" check for invalid (non-UTF8) characters in "
"recipe metadata variable values (i.e. :term:`DESCRIPTION`, "
":term:`SUMMARY`, :term:`LICENSE`, and :term:`SECTION`). Some package "
"managers do not support these characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:247
msgid ""
"Added an \"invalid-packageconfig\" check for any options specified in "
":term:`PACKAGECONFIG` that do not match any :term:`PACKAGECONFIG` option "
"defined for the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:256
#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:355
msgid "These additional changes exist:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:258
msgid "``gtk-update-icon-cache`` has been renamed to ``gtk-icon-utils``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:260
msgid ""
"The ``tools-profile`` :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` item as well as its "
"corresponding packagegroup and ``packagegroup-core-tools-profile`` no "
"longer bring in ``oprofile``. Bringing in ``oprofile`` was originally "
"added to aid compilation on resource-constrained targets. However, this "
"aid has not been widely used and is not likely to be used going forward "
"due to the more powerful target platforms and the existence of better "
"cross-compilation tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:269
msgid ""
"The :term:`IMAGE_FSTYPES` variable's default value now specifies ``ext4``"
" instead of ``ext3``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:272
msgid "All support for the ``PRINC`` variable has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.0.rst:274
msgid ""
"The ``packagegroup-core-full-cmdline`` packagegroup no longer brings in "
"``lighttpd`` due to the fact that bringing in ``lighttpd`` is not really "
"in line with the packagegroup's purpose, which is to add full versions of"
" command-line tools that by default are provided by ``busybox``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:4
msgid "Release 2.1 (krogoth)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:6
msgid ""
"This section provides migration information for moving to the Yocto "
"Project 2.1 Release (codename \"krogoth\") from the prior release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:12
msgid "Variable Expansion in Python Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:14
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Variable expressions, such as ``${VARNAME}`` no longer expand "
"automatically within Python functions. Suppressing expansion was done to "
"allow Python functions to construct shell scripts or other code for "
"situations in which you do not want such expressions expanded. For any "
"existing code that relies on these expansions, you need to change the "
"expansions to expand the value of individual variables through "
"``d.getVar()``. To alternatively expand more complex expressions, use "
"``d.expand()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:26
msgid "Overrides Must Now be Lower-Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:28
msgid ""
"The convention for overrides has always been for them to be lower-case "
"characters. This practice is now a requirement as BitBake's datastore now"
" assumes lower-case characters in order to give a slight performance "
"boost during parsing. In practical terms, this requirement means that "
"anything that ends up in :term:`OVERRIDES` must now appear in lower-case "
"characters (e.g. values for :term:`MACHINE`, :term:`TARGET_ARCH`, "
":term:`DISTRO`, and also recipe names if ``_pn-``\\ recipename overrides "
"are to be effective)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:40
msgid "Expand Parameter to ``getVar()`` and ``getVarFlag()`` is Now Mandatory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:42
msgid ""
"The expand parameter to ``getVar()`` and ``getVarFlag()`` previously "
"defaulted to False if not specified. Now, however, no default exists so "
"one must be specified. You must change any ``getVar()`` calls that do not"
" specify the final expand parameter to calls that do specify the "
"parameter. You can run the following ``sed`` command at the base of a "
"layer to make this change::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:54
msgid ""
"The reason for this change is that it prepares the way for changing the "
"default to True in a future Yocto Project release. This future change is "
"a much more sensible default than False. However, the change needs to be "
"made gradually as a sudden change of the default would potentially cause "
"side-effects that would be difficult to detect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:64
msgid "Makefile Environment Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:66
msgid ""
":term:`EXTRA_OEMAKE` now defaults to \"\" instead of \"-e MAKEFLAGS=\". "
"Setting :term:`EXTRA_OEMAKE` to \"-e MAKEFLAGS=\" by default was a "
"historical accident that has required many classes (e.g. :ref:`ref-"
"classes-autotools`, ``module``) and recipes to override this default in "
"order to work with sensible build systems. When upgrading to the release,"
" you must edit any recipe that relies upon this old default by either "
"setting :term:`EXTRA_OEMAKE` back to \"-e MAKEFLAGS=\" or by explicitly "
"setting any required variable value overrides using :term:`EXTRA_OEMAKE`,"
" which is typically only needed when a Makefile sets a default value for "
"a variable that is inappropriate for cross-compilation using the \"=\" "
"operator rather than the \"?=\" operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``libexecdir`` Reverted to ``${prefix}/libexec``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:83
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The use of ``${libdir}/${BPN}`` as ``libexecdir`` is different as "
"compared to all other mainstream distributions, which either uses "
"``${prefix}/libexec`` or ``${libdir}``. The use is also contrary to the "
"GNU Coding Standards (i.e. https://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/html_node"
"/Directory-Variables.html) that suggest ``${prefix}/libexec`` and also "
"notes that any package-specific nesting should be done by the package "
"itself. Finally, having ``libexecdir`` change between recipes makes it "
"very difficult for different recipes to invoke binaries that have been "
"installed into ``libexecdir``. The Filesystem Hierarchy Standard (i.e. "
"https://refspecs.linuxfoundation.org/FHS_3.0/fhs/ch04s07.html) now "
"recognizes the use of ``${prefix}/libexec/``, giving distributions the "
"choice between ``${prefix}/lib`` or ``${prefix}/libexec`` without "
"breaking FHS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:101
msgid "``ac_cv_sizeof_off_t`` is No Longer Cached in Site Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:103
msgid ""
"For recipes inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-autotools` class, "
"``ac_cv_sizeof_off_t`` is no longer cached in the site files for "
"``autoconf``. The reason for this change is because the "
"``ac_cv_sizeof_off_t`` value is not necessarily static per architecture "
"as was previously assumed. Rather, the value changes based on whether "
"large file support is enabled. For most software that uses ``autoconf``, "
"this change should not be a problem. However, if you have a recipe that "
"bypasses the standard :ref:`ref-tasks-configure` task from the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-autotools` class and the software the recipe is building uses a "
"very old version of ``autoconf``, the recipe might be incapable of "
"determining the correct size of ``off_t`` during :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"configure`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:115
msgid ""
"The best course of action is to patch the software as necessary to allow "
"the default implementation from the :ref:`ref-classes-autotools` class to"
" work such that ``autoreconf`` succeeds and produces a working configure "
"script, and to remove the overridden :ref:`ref-tasks-configure` task such"
" that the default implementation does get used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:124
msgid "Image Generation is Now Split Out from Filesystem Generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:126
msgid ""
"Previously, for image recipes the :ref:`ref-tasks-rootfs` task assembled "
"the filesystem and then from that filesystem generated images. With this "
"Yocto Project release, image generation is split into separate :ref:`ref-"
"tasks-image` tasks for clarity both in operation and in the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:132
msgid ""
"For most cases, this change does not present any problems. However, if "
"you have made customizations that directly modify the :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"rootfs` task or that mention :ref:`ref-tasks-rootfs`, you might need to "
"update those changes. In particular, if you had added any tasks after "
":ref:`ref-tasks-rootfs`, you should make edits so that those tasks are "
"after the :ref:`ref-tasks-image-complete` task rather than after :ref"
":`ref-tasks-rootfs` so that your added tasks run at the correct time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:141
msgid ""
"A minor part of this restructuring is that the post-processing "
"definitions and functions have been moved from the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"image` class to the :ref:`rootfs-postcommands <ref-classes-rootfs*>` "
"class. Functionally, however, they remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:151
msgid "The following recipes have been removed in the 2.1 release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:153
msgid "``gcc`` version 4.8: Versions 4.9 and 5.3 remain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:155
msgid ""
"``qt4``: All support for Qt 4.x has been moved out to a separate ``meta-"
"qt4`` layer because Qt 4 is no longer supported upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:158
msgid "``x11vnc``: Moved to the ``meta-oe`` layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:160
msgid "``linux-yocto-3.14``: No longer supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:162
msgid "``linux-yocto-3.19``: No longer supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:164
msgid "``libjpeg``: Replaced by the ``libjpeg-turbo`` recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:166
msgid "``pth``: Became obsolete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:168
msgid ""
"``liboil``: Recipe is no longer needed and has been moved to the ``meta-"
"multimedia`` layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:171
msgid ""
"``gtk-theme-torturer``: Recipe is no longer needed and has been moved to "
"the ``meta-gnome`` layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:174
msgid ""
"``gnome-mime-data``: Recipe is no longer needed and has been moved to the"
" ``meta-gnome`` layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:177
msgid ""
"``udev``: Replaced by the ``eudev`` recipe for compatibility when using "
"``sysvinit`` with newer kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:180
msgid "``python-pygtk``: Recipe became obsolete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:182
msgid ""
"``adt-installer``: Recipe became obsolete. See the \":ref:`migration-"
"guides/migration-2.1:adt removed`\" section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:188
msgid "Class Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:190
msgid "The following classes have changed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:192
msgid ""
"``autotools_stage``: Removed because the :ref:`ref-classes-autotools` "
"class now provides its functionality. Recipes that inherited from "
"``autotools_stage`` should now inherit from :ref:`ref-classes-autotools` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:197
msgid ""
"``boot-directdisk``: Merged into the ``image-vm`` class. The ``boot-"
"directdisk`` class was rarely directly used. Consequently, this change "
"should not cause any issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:201
msgid ""
"``bootimg``: Merged into the :ref:`ref-classes-image-live` class. The "
"``bootimg`` class was rarely directly used. Consequently, this change "
"should not cause any issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:205
msgid ""
"``packageinfo``: Removed due to its limited use by the Hob UI, which has "
"itself been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:211
msgid "Build System User Interface Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:213
msgid "The following changes have been made to the build system user interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:215
msgid ""
"*Hob GTK+-based UI*: Removed because it is unmaintained and based on the "
"outdated GTK+ 2 library. The Toaster web-based UI is much more capable "
"and is actively maintained. See the \":ref:`toaster-manual/setup-and-"
"use:using the toaster web interface`\" section in the Toaster User Manual"
" for more information on this interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:222
msgid ""
"*\"puccho\" BitBake UI*: Removed because is unmaintained and no longer "
"useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:228
msgid "ADT Removed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:230
msgid ""
"The Application Development Toolkit (ADT) has been removed because its "
"functionality almost completely overlapped with the :ref:`standard SDK "
"<sdk-manual/using:using the standard sdk>` and the :ref:`extensible SDK "
"<sdk-manual/extensible:using the extensible sdk>`. For information on "
"these SDKs and how to build and use them, see the :doc:`/sdk-"
"manual/index` manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:239
msgid ""
"The Yocto Project Eclipse IDE Plug-in is still supported and is not "
"affected by this change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:245
msgid "Poky Reference Distribution Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:247
msgid "The following changes have been made for the Poky distribution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:249
msgid ""
"The ``meta-yocto`` layer has been renamed to ``meta-poky`` to better "
"match its purpose, which is to provide the Poky reference distribution. "
"The ``meta-yocto-bsp`` layer retains its original name since it provides "
"reference machines for the Yocto Project and it is otherwise unrelated to"
" Poky. References to ``meta-yocto`` in your :ref:`structure-build-conf-"
"bblayers.conf` should automatically be updated, so you should not need to"
" change anything unless you are relying on this naming elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:258
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-uninative` class is now enabled by default in Poky."
" This class attempts to isolate the build system from the host "
"distribution's C library and makes re-use of native shared state "
"artifacts across different host distributions practical. With this class "
"enabled, a tarball containing a pre-built C library is downloaded at the "
"start of the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:265
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-uninative` class is enabled through the "
"``meta/conf/distro/include/yocto-uninative.inc`` file, which for those "
"not using the Poky distribution, can include to easily enable the same "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:270
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if you wish to build your own ``uninative`` tarball, you "
"can do so by building the ``uninative-tarball`` recipe, making it "
"available to your build machines (e.g. over HTTP/HTTPS) and setting a "
"similar configuration as the one set by ``yocto-uninative.inc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:275
msgid ""
"Static library generation, for most cases, is now disabled by default in "
"the Poky distribution. Disabling this generation saves some build time as"
" well as the size used for build output artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:279
msgid ""
"Disabling this library generation is accomplished through a "
"``meta/conf/distro/include/no-static-libs.inc``, which for those not "
"using the Poky distribution can easily include to enable the same "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:284
msgid ""
"Any recipe that needs to opt-out of having the ``--disable-static`` "
"option specified on the configure command line either because it is not a"
" supported option for the configure script or because static libraries "
"are needed should set the following variable::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:291
msgid ""
"The separate ``poky-tiny`` distribution now uses the musl C library "
"instead of a heavily pared down ``glibc``. Using musl results in a "
"smaller distribution and facilitates much greater maintainability because"
" musl is designed to have a small footprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:296
msgid ""
"If you have used ``poky-tiny`` and have customized the ``glibc`` "
"configuration you will need to redo those customizations with musl when "
"upgrading to the new release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:305
msgid "The following changes have been made to packaging:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:307
msgid ""
"The ``runuser`` and ``mountpoint`` binaries, which were previously in the"
" main ``util-linux`` package, have been split out into the ``util-linux-"
"runuser`` and ``util-linux-mountpoint`` packages, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:312
msgid ""
"The ``python-elementtree`` package has been merged into the ``python-"
"xml`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:318
msgid "Tuning File Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:320
msgid "The following changes have been made to the tuning files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:322
msgid ""
"The \"no-thumb-interwork\" tuning feature has been dropped from the ARM "
"tune include files. Because interworking is required for ARM EABI, "
"attempting to disable it through a tuning feature no longer makes sense."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:329
msgid "Support for ARM OABI was deprecated in gcc 4.7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:331
msgid ""
"The ``tune-cortexm*.inc`` and ``tune-cortexr4.inc`` files have been "
"removed because they are poorly tested. Until the OpenEmbedded build "
"system officially gains support for CPUs without an MMU, these tuning "
"files would probably be better maintained in a separate layer if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:340
msgid "Supporting GObject Introspection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:342
msgid ""
"This release supports generation of GLib Introspective Repository (GIR) "
"files through GObject introspection, which is the standard mechanism for "
"accessing GObject-based software from runtime environments. You can "
"enable, disable, and test the generation of this data. See the \":ref"
":`dev-manual/gobject-introspection:enabling gobject introspection "
"support`\" section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual for more"
" information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:357
msgid ""
"The minimum Git version has been increased to 1.8.3.1. If your host "
"distribution does not provide a sufficiently recent version, you can "
"install the :term:`buildtools`, which will provide it. See the :ref:`ref-"
"manual/system-requirements:required git, tar, python, make and gcc "
"versions` section for more information on the :term:`buildtools` tarball."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:363
msgid ""
"The buggy and incomplete support for the RPM version 4 package manager "
"has been removed. The well-tested and maintained support for RPM version "
"5 remains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:367
msgid ""
"Previously, the following list of packages were removed if package-"
"management was not in :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES`, regardless of any "
"dependencies::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:378
msgid ""
"With the Yocto Project 2.1 release, these packages are only removed if "
"\"read-only-rootfs\" is in :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES`, since they might still"
" be needed for a read-write image even in the absence of a package "
"manager (e.g. if users need to be added, modified, or removed at "
"runtime)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:384
msgid ""
"The :ref:`devtool modify <dev-manual/devtool:use \\`\\`devtool "
"modify\\`\\` to modify the source of an existing component>` command now "
"defaults to extracting the source since that is most commonly expected. "
"The ``-x`` or ``--extract`` options are now no-ops. If you wish to "
"provide your own existing source tree, you will now need to specify "
"either the ``-n`` or ``--no-extract`` options when running ``devtool "
"modify``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:392
msgid ""
"If the formfactor for a machine is either not supplied or does not "
"specify whether a keyboard is attached, then the default is to assume a "
"keyboard is attached rather than assume no keyboard. This change "
"primarily affects the Sato UI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:397
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The ``.debug`` directory packaging is now automatic. If your recipe "
"builds software that installs binaries into directories other than the "
"standard ones, you no longer need to take care of setting "
"``FILES_${PN}-dbg`` to pick up the resulting ``.debug`` directories as "
"these directories are automatically found and added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:403
msgid ""
"Inaccurate disk and CPU percentage data has been dropped from :ref:`ref-"
"classes-buildstats` output. This data has been replaced with "
"``getrusage()`` data and corrected IO statistics. You will probably need "
"to update any custom code that reads the :ref:`ref-classes-buildstats` "
"data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:408
msgid ""
"The ``meta/conf/distro/include/package_regex.inc`` is now deprecated. The"
" contents of this file have been moved to individual recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:413
msgid ""
"Because this file will likely be removed in a future Yocto Project "
"release, it is suggested that you remove any references to the file that "
"might be in your configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:417
msgid ""
"The ``v86d/uvesafb`` has been removed from the ``genericx86`` and "
"``genericx86-64`` reference machines, which are provided by the ``meta-"
"yocto-bsp`` layer. Most modern x86 boards do not rely on this file and it"
" only adds kernel error messages during startup. If you do still need to "
"support ``uvesafb``, you can simply add ``v86d`` to your image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.1.rst:424
msgid ""
"Build sysroot paths are now removed from debug symbol files. Removing "
"these paths means that remote GDB using an unstripped build system "
"sysroot will no longer work (although this was never documented to work)."
" The supported method to accomplish something similar is to set "
"``IMAGE_GEN_DEBUGFS`` to \"1\", which will generate a companion debug "
"image containing unstripped binaries and associated debug sources "
"alongside the image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:4
msgid "Release 2.2 (morty)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:6
msgid ""
"This section provides migration information for moving to the Yocto "
"Project 2.2 Release (codename \"morty\") from the prior release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:12
msgid "Minimum Kernel Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:14
msgid ""
"The minimum kernel version for the target system and for SDK is now "
"3.2.0, due to the upgrade to ``glibc 2.24``. Specifically, for "
"AArch64-based targets the version is 3.14. For Nios II-based targets, the"
" minimum kernel version is 3.19."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:21
msgid ""
"For x86 and x86_64, you can reset :term:`OLDEST_KERNEL` to anything down "
"to 2.6.32 if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:27
msgid "Staging Directories in Sysroot Has Been Simplified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:29
msgid ""
"The way directories are staged in sysroot has been simplified and "
"introduces the new :term:`SYSROOT_DIRS`, :term:`SYSROOT_DIRS_NATIVE`, and"
" ``SYSROOT_DIRS_BLACKLIST`` (replaced by :term:`SYSROOT_DIRS_IGNORE` in "
"version 4.0). See the :oe_lists:`v2 patch series on the OE-Core Mailing "
"List </pipermail/openembedded-core/2016-May/121365.html>` for additional "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:40
msgid "Removal of Old Images and Other Files in ``tmp/deploy`` Now Enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:42
msgid ""
"Removal of old images and other files in ``tmp/deploy/`` is now enabled "
"by default due to a new staging method used for those files. As a result "
"of this change, the ``RM_OLD_IMAGE`` variable is now redundant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:49
msgid "Python Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:51
msgid "The following changes for Python occurred:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:56
msgid "BitBake Now Requires Python 3.4+"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:58
msgid "BitBake requires Python 3.4 or greater."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:63
msgid "UTF-8 Locale Required on Build Host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:65
msgid ""
"A UTF-8 locale is required on the build host due to Python 3. Since "
"C.UTF-8 is not a standard, the default is en_US.UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:71
msgid "Metadata Must Now Use Python 3 Syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:73
msgid ""
"The metadata is now required to use Python 3 syntax. For help preparing "
"metadata, see any of the many Python 3 porting guides available. "
"Alternatively, you can reference the conversion commits for BitBake and "
"you can use :term:`OpenEmbedded-Core (OE-Core)` as a guide for changes. "
"Particular areas of interest are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:79
msgid "subprocess command-line pipes needing locale decoding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:81
msgid "the syntax for octal values changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:83
msgid "the ``iter*()`` functions changed name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:85
msgid "iterators now return views, not lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:87
msgid "changed names for Python modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:92
msgid "Target Python Recipes Switched to Python 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:94
msgid ""
"Most target Python recipes have now been switched to Python 3. "
"Unfortunately, systems using RPM as a package manager and providing "
"online package-manager support through SMART still require Python 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:100
msgid ""
"Python 2 and recipes that use it can still be built for the target as "
"with previous versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:106
msgid "``buildtools-tarball`` Includes Python 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:108
msgid "The :term:`buildtools` tarball now includes Python 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:113
msgid "uClibc Replaced by musl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:115
msgid ""
"uClibc has been removed in favor of musl. Musl has matured, is better "
"maintained, and is compatible with a wider range of applications as "
"compared to uClibc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.2.rst:122
