#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:4
msgid "Release 2.3 (pyro)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:6
msgid ""
"This section provides migration information for moving to the Yocto "
"Project 2.3 Release (codename \"pyro\") from the prior release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:12
msgid "Recipe-specific Sysroots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:14
msgid ""
"The OpenEmbedded build system now uses one sysroot per recipe to resolve "
"long-standing issues with configuration script auto-detection of "
"undeclared dependencies. Consequently, you might find that some of your "
"previously written custom recipes are missing declared dependencies, "
"particularly those dependencies that are incidentally built earlier in a "
"typical build process and thus are already likely to be present in the "
"shared sysroot in previous releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:22
msgid "Consider the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:24
msgid ""
"*Declare Build-Time Dependencies:* Because of this new feature, you must "
"explicitly declare all build-time dependencies for your recipe. If you do"
" not declare these dependencies, they are not populated into the sysroot "
"for the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:29
msgid ""
"*Specify Pre-Installation and Post-Installation Native Tool "
"Dependencies:* You must specifically specify any special native tool "
"dependencies of ``pkg_preinst`` and ``pkg_postinst`` scripts by using the"
" :term:`PACKAGE_WRITE_DEPS` variable. Specifying these dependencies "
"ensures that these tools are available if these scripts need to be run on"
" the build host during the :ref:`ref-tasks-rootfs` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:37
msgid ""
"As an example, see the ``dbus`` recipe. You will see that this recipe has"
" a ``pkg_postinst`` that calls ``systemctl`` if \"systemd\" is in "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`. In the example, ``systemd-systemctl-native`` is "
"added to :term:`PACKAGE_WRITE_DEPS`, which is also conditional on "
"\"systemd\" being in :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:43
msgid ""
"Examine Recipes that Use ``SSTATEPOSTINSTFUNCS``: You need to examine any"
" recipe that uses ``SSTATEPOSTINSTFUNCS`` and determine steps to take."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:47
msgid ""
"Functions added to ``SSTATEPOSTINSTFUNCS`` are still called as they were "
"in previous Yocto Project releases. However, since a separate sysroot is "
"now being populated for every recipe and if existing functions being "
"called through ``SSTATEPOSTINSTFUNCS`` are doing relocation, then you "
"will need to change these to use a post-installation script that is "
"installed by a function added to :term:`SYSROOT_PREPROCESS_FUNCS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:55
msgid ""
"For an example, see the :ref:`ref-classes-pixbufcache` class in "
"``meta/classes/`` in the :ref:`overview-manual/development-"
"environment:yocto project source repositories`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:60
msgid ""
"The SSTATEPOSTINSTFUNCS variable itself is now deprecated in favor of the"
" do_populate_sysroot[postfuncs] task. Consequently, if you do still have "
"any function or functions that need to be called after the sysroot "
"component is created for a recipe, then you would be well advised to take"
" steps to use a post installation script as described previously. Taking "
"these steps prepares your code for when SSTATEPOSTINSTFUNCS is removed in"
" a future Yocto Project release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:72
msgid ""
"*Specify the Sysroot when Using Certain External Scripts:* Because the "
"shared sysroot is now gone, the scripts ``oe-find-native-sysroot`` and "
"``oe-run-native`` have been changed such that you need to specify which "
"recipe's :term:`STAGING_DIR_NATIVE` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:80
msgid ""
"You can find more information on how recipe-specific sysroots work in the"
" \":ref:`ref-classes-staging`\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:86
msgid "``PATH`` Variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:88
msgid ""
"Within the environment used to run build tasks, the environment variable "
"``PATH`` is now sanitized such that the normal native binary paths "
"(``/bin``, ``/sbin``, ``/usr/bin`` and so forth) are removed and a "
"directory containing symbolic links linking only to the binaries from the"
" host mentioned in the :term:`HOSTTOOLS` and :term:`HOSTTOOLS_NONFATAL` "
"variables is added to ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:96
msgid ""
"Consequently, any native binaries provided by the host that you need to "
"call needs to be in one of these two variables at the configuration "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:100
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can add a native recipe (i.e. ``-native``) that "
"provides the binary to the recipe's :term:`DEPENDS` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:106
msgid ""
"PATH is not sanitized in the same way within ``devshell``. If it were, "
"you would have difficulty running host tools for development and "
"debugging within the shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:114
msgid "Changes to Scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:116
msgid "The following changes to scripts took place:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:118
msgid ""
"``oe-find-native-sysroot``: The usage for the ``oe-find-native-sysroot`` "
"script has changed to the following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:123
msgid ""
"You must now supply a recipe for recipe as part of the command. Prior to "
"the Yocto Project 2.3 release, it was not necessary to provide the script"
" with the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:127
msgid ""
"``oe-run-native``: The usage for the ``oe-run-native`` script has changed"
" to the following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:132
msgid ""
"You must supply the name of the native recipe and the tool you want to "
"run as part of the command. Prior to the Yocto Project 2.3 release, it "
"was not necessary to provide the native recipe with the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:137
msgid ""
"``cleanup-workdir``: The ``cleanup-workdir`` script has been removed "
"because the script was found to be deleting files it should not have, "
"which lead to broken build trees. Rather than trying to delete portions "
"of :term:`TMPDIR` and getting it wrong, it is recommended that you delete"
" :term:`TMPDIR` and have it restored from shared state (sstate) on "
"subsequent builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:144
msgid ""
"``wipe-sysroot``: The ``wipe-sysroot`` script has been removed as it is "
"no longer needed with recipe-specific sysroots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:150
msgid "Changes to Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:152
msgid ""
"The previously deprecated ``bb.data.getVar()``, ``bb.data.setVar()``, and"
" related functions have been removed in favor of ``d.getVar()``, "
"``d.setVar()``, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:156
msgid "You need to fix any references to these old functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:165
msgid ""
"*BitBake's Graphical Dependency Explorer UI Replaced:* BitBake's "
"graphical dependency explorer UI ``depexp`` was replaced by ``taskexp`` "
"(\"Task Explorer\"), which provides a graphical way of exploring the "
"``task-depends.dot`` file. The data presented by Task Explorer is much "
"more accurate than the data that was presented by ``depexp``. Being able "
"to visualize the data is an often requested feature as standard ``*.dot``"
" file viewers cannot usual cope with the size of the ``task-depends.dot``"
" file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:174
msgid ""
"*BitBake \"-g\" Output Changes:* The ``package-depends.dot`` and ``pn-"
"depends.dot`` files as previously generated using the ``bitbake -g`` "
"command have been removed. A ``recipe-depends.dot`` file is now generated"
" as a collapsed version of ``task-depends.dot`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:180
msgid ""
"The reason for this change is because ``package-depends.dot`` and ``pn-"
"depends.dot`` largely date back to a time before task-based execution and"
" do not take into account task-level dependencies between recipes, which "
"could be misleading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:185
msgid ""
"*Mirror Variable Splitting Changes:* Mirror variables including "
":term:`MIRRORS`, :term:`PREMIRRORS`, and :term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` can now "
"separate values entirely with spaces. Consequently, you no longer need "
"\"\\\\n\". BitBake looks for pairs of values, which simplifies usage. "
"There should be no change required to existing mirror variable values "
"themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:193
msgid ""
"*The Subversion (SVN) Fetcher Uses an \"ssh\" Parameter and Not an "
"\"rsh\" Parameter:* The SVN fetcher now takes an \"ssh\" parameter "
"instead of an \"rsh\" parameter. This new optional parameter is used when"
" the \"protocol\" parameter is set to \"svn+ssh\". You can only use the "
"new parameter to specify the ``ssh`` program used by SVN. The SVN fetcher"
" passes the new parameter through the ``SVN_SSH`` environment variable "
"during the :ref:`ref-tasks-fetch` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:201
msgid ""
"See the \":ref:`bitbake-user-manual/bitbake-user-manual-"
"fetching:subversion (svn) fetcher (\\`\\`svn://\\`\\`)`\" section in the "
"BitBake User Manual for additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:205
msgid ""
"``BB_SETSCENE_VERIFY_FUNCTION`` and ``BB_SETSCENE_VERIFY_FUNCTION2`` "
"Removed: Because the mechanism they were part of is no longer necessary "
"with recipe-specific sysroots, the ``BB_SETSCENE_VERIFY_FUNCTION`` and "
"``BB_SETSCENE_VERIFY_FUNCTION2`` variables have been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:214
msgid "Absolute Symbolic Links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:216
msgid ""
"Absolute symbolic links (symlinks) within staged files are no longer "
"permitted and now trigger an error. Any explicit creation of symlinks can"
" use the ``lnr`` script, which is a replacement for ``ln -r``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:220
msgid ""
"If the build scripts in the software that the recipe is building are "
"creating a number of absolute symlinks that need to be corrected, you can"
" inherit ``relative_symlinks`` within the recipe to turn those absolute "
"symlinks into relative symlinks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:228
msgid "GPLv2 Versions of GPLv3 Recipes Moved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:230
msgid ""
"Older GPLv2 versions of GPLv3 recipes have moved to a separate ``meta-"
"gplv2`` layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:233
msgid ""
"If you use :term:`INCOMPATIBLE_LICENSE` to exclude GPLv3 or set "
":term:`PREFERRED_VERSION` to substitute a GPLv2 version of a GPLv3 "
"recipe, then you must add the ``meta-gplv2`` layer to your configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:240
msgid ""
"You can ``find meta-gplv2`` layer in the OpenEmbedded layer index at "
":oe_layer:`/meta-gplv2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:243
msgid ""
"These relocated GPLv2 recipes do not receive the same level of "
"maintenance as other core recipes. The recipes do not get security fixes "
"and upstream no longer maintains them. In fact, the upstream community is"
" actively hostile towards people that use the old versions of the "
"recipes. Moving these recipes into a separate layer both makes the "
"different needs of the recipes clearer and clearly identifies the number "
"of these recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:253
msgid ""
"The long-term solution might be to move to BSD-licensed replacements of "
"the GPLv3 components for those that need to exclude GPLv3-licensed "
"components from the target system. This solution will be investigated for"
" future Yocto Project releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:261
msgid "Package Management Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:263
msgid "The following package management changes took place:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:265
msgid ""
"Smart package manager is replaced by DNF package manager. Smart has "
"become unmaintained upstream, is not ported to Python 3.x. Consequently, "
"Smart needed to be replaced. DNF is the only feasible candidate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:270
msgid ""
"The change in functionality is that the on-target runtime package "
"management from remote package feeds is now done with a different tool "
"that has a different set of command-line options. If you have scripts "
"that call the tool directly, or use its API, they need to be fixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:276
msgid ""
"For more information, see the `DNF Documentation "
"<https://dnf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:279
msgid "Rpm 5.x is replaced with Rpm 4.x. This is done for two major reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:281
msgid ""
"DNF is API-incompatible with Rpm 5.x and porting it and maintaining the "
"port is non-trivial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:284
msgid ""
"Rpm 5.x itself has limited maintenance upstream, and the Yocto Project is"
" one of the very few remaining users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:287
msgid "Berkeley DB 6.x is removed and Berkeley DB 5.x becomes the default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:289
msgid ""
"Version 6.x of Berkeley DB has largely been rejected by the open source "
"community due to its AGPLv3 license. As a result, most mainstream open "
"source projects that require DB are still developed and tested with DB "
"5.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:294
msgid ""
"In OE-core, the only thing that was requiring DB 6.x was Rpm 5.x. Thus, "
"no reason exists to continue carrying DB 6.x in OE-core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:297
msgid "``createrepo`` is replaced with ``createrepo_c``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:299
msgid ""
"``createrepo_c`` is the current incarnation of the tool that generates "
"remote repository metadata. It is written in C as compared to "
"``createrepo``, which is written in Python. ``createrepo_c`` is faster "
"and is maintained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:304
msgid "Architecture-independent RPM packages are \"noarch\" instead of \"all\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:306
msgid ""
"This change was made because too many places in DNF/RPM4 stack already "
"make that assumption. Only the filenames and the architecture tag has "
"changed. Nothing else has changed in OE-core system, particularly in the "
":ref:`ref-classes-allarch` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:311
msgid ""
"Signing of remote package feeds using ``PACKAGE_FEED_SIGN`` is not "
"currently supported. This issue will be fully addressed in a future Yocto"
" Project release. See :yocto_bugs:`defect 11209 </show_bug.cgi?id=11209>`"
" for more information on a solution to package feed signing with RPM in "
"the Yocto Project 2.3 release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:317
msgid ""
"OPKG now uses the libsolv backend for resolving package dependencies by "
"default. This is vastly superior to OPKG's internal ad-hoc solver that "
"was previously used. This change does have a small impact on disk (around"
" 500 KB) and memory footprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:324
msgid ""
"For further details on this change, see the :yocto_git:`commit message "
"</poky/commit/?id=f4d4f99cfbc2396e49c1613a7d237b9e57f06f81>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:334
msgid ""
"``linux-yocto 4.8``: Version 4.8 has been removed. Versions 4.1 (LTSI), "
"4.4 (LTS), 4.9 (LTS/LTSI) and 4.10 are now present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:337
msgid "``python-smartpm``: Functionally replaced by ``dnf``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:339
msgid "``createrepo``: Replaced by the ``createrepo-c`` recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:341
msgid ""
"``rpmresolve``: No longer needed with the move to RPM 4 as RPM itself is "
"used instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:344
msgid ""
"``gstreamer``: Removed the GStreamer Git version recipes as they have "
"been stale. ``1.10.``\\ x recipes are still present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:347
msgid ""
"``alsa-conf-base``: Merged into ``alsa-conf`` since ``libasound`` "
"depended on both. Essentially, no way existed to install only one of "
"these."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:351
msgid ""
"``tremor``: Moved to ``meta-multimedia``. Fixed-integer Vorbis decoding "
"is not needed by current hardware. Thus, GStreamer's ivorbis plugin has "
"been disabled by default eliminating the need for the ``tremor`` recipe "
"in :term:`OpenEmbedded-Core (OE-Core)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:356
msgid "``gummiboot``: Replaced by ``systemd-boot``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:361
msgid "Wic Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:363
msgid "The following changes have been made to Wic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:367
msgid ""
"For more information on Wic, see the \":ref:`dev-manual/wic:creating "
"partitioned images using wic`\" section in the Yocto Project Development "
"Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:371
msgid ""
"*Default Output Directory Changed:* Wic's default output directory is now"
" the current directory by default instead of the unusual "
"``/var/tmp/wic``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:375
msgid ""
"The ``-o`` and ``--outdir`` options remain unchanged and are used to "
"specify your preferred output directory if you do not want to use the "
"default directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:379
msgid ""
"*fsimage Plug-in Removed:* The Wic fsimage plugin has been removed as it "
"duplicates functionality of the rawcopy plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:385
msgid "QA Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:387
msgid "The following QA checks have changed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:389
msgid ""
"``unsafe-references-in-binaries``: The ``unsafe-references-in-binaries`` "
"QA check, which was disabled by default, has now been removed. This check"
" was intended to detect binaries in ``/bin`` that link to libraries in "
"``/usr/lib`` and have the case where the user has ``/usr`` on a separate "
"filesystem to ``/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:396
msgid ""
"The removed QA check was buggy. Additionally, ``/usr`` residing on a "
"separate partition from ``/`` is now a rare configuration. Consequently, "
"``unsafe-references-in-binaries`` was removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:400
msgid ""
"``file-rdeps``: The ``file-rdeps`` QA check is now an error by default "
"instead of a warning. Because it is an error instead of a warning, you "
"need to address missing runtime dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:404
msgid ""
"For additional information, see the :ref:`ref-classes-insane` class and "
"the \":ref:`ref-manual/qa-checks:errors and warnings`\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:415
msgid ""
"In this release, a number of recipes have been changed to ignore the "
"``largefile`` :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` item, enabling large file support "
"unconditionally. This feature has always been enabled by default. "
"Disabling the feature has not been widely tested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:423
msgid ""
"Future releases of the Yocto Project will remove entirely the ability to "
"disable the largefile feature, which would make it unconditionally "
"enabled everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:428
msgid ""
"If the :term:`DISTRO_VERSION` value contains the value of the "
":term:`DATE` variable, which is the default between Poky releases, the "
":term:`DATE` value is explicitly excluded from ``/etc/issue`` and "
"``/etc/issue.net``, which is displayed at the login prompt, in order to "
"avoid conflicts with Multilib enabled. Regardless, the :term:`DATE` value"
" is inaccurate if the ``base-files`` recipe is restored from shared state"
" (sstate) rather than rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:437
msgid ""
"If you need the build date recorded in ``/etc/issue*`` or anywhere else "
"in your image, a better method is to define a post-processing function to"
" do it and have the function called from "
":term:`ROOTFS_POSTPROCESS_COMMAND`. Doing so ensures the value is always "
"up-to-date with the created image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:444
msgid ""
"Dropbear's ``init`` script now disables DSA host keys by default. This "
"change is in line with the systemd service file, which supports RSA keys "
"only, and with recent versions of OpenSSH, which deprecates DSA host "
"keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:449
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-buildhistory` class now correctly uses tabs as "
"separators between all columns in ``installed-package-sizes.txt`` in "
"order to aid import into other tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:454
msgid ""
"The ``USE_LDCONFIG`` variable has been replaced with the \"ldconfig\" "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` feature. Distributions that previously set::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:459
msgid "should now instead use the following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:463
msgid ""
"The default value of :term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_INCLUDE` now includes all "
"versions of AGPL licenses in addition to GPL and LGPL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:469
msgid ""
"The default list is not intended to be guaranteed as a complete safe "
"list. You should seek legal advice based on what you are distributing if "
"you are unsure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:473
msgid ""
"Kernel module packages are now suffixed with the kernel version in order "
"to allow module packages from multiple kernel versions to co-exist on a "
"target system. If you wish to return to the previous naming scheme that "
"does not include the version suffix, use the following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:481
msgid ""
"Removal of ``libtool`` ``*.la`` files is now enabled by default. The "
"``*.la`` files are not actually needed on Linux and relocating them is an"
" unnecessary burden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:485
msgid ""
"If you need to preserve these ``.la`` files (e.g. in a custom "
"distribution), you must change :term:`INHERIT_DISTRO` such that \":ref"
":`ref-classes-remove-libtool`\" is not included in the value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:490
msgid ""
"Extensible SDKs built for GCC 5+ now refuse to install on a distribution "
"where the host GCC version is 4.8 or 4.9. This change resulted from the "
"fact that the installation is known to fail due to the way the "
"``uninative`` shared state (sstate) package is built. See the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-uninative` class for additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:496
msgid ""
"All :ref:`ref-classes-native` and :ref:`ref-classes-nativesdk` recipes "
"now use a separate :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` value instead of sharing the "
"value used by recipes for the target, in order to avoid unnecessary "
"rebuilds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:500
msgid ""
"The :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` for :ref:`ref-classes-native` recipes is "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES_NATIVE` added to an intersection of "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` and :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES_FILTER_NATIVE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:504
msgid ""
"For :ref:`ref-classes-nativesdk` recipes, the corresponding variables are"
" :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES_NATIVESDK` and "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES_FILTER_NATIVESDK`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:508
msgid ""
"The ``FILESDIR`` variable, which was previously deprecated and rarely "
"used, has now been removed. You should change any recipes that set "
"``FILESDIR`` to set :term:`FILESPATH` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.3.rst:512
msgid ""
"The ``MULTIMACH_HOST_SYS`` variable has been removed as it is no longer "
"needed with recipe-specific sysroots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:4
msgid "Release 2.4 (rocko)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:6
msgid ""
"This section provides migration information for moving to the Yocto "
"Project 2.4 Release (codename \"rocko\") from the prior release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:12
msgid "Memory Resident Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:14
msgid ""
"A persistent mode is now available in BitBake's default operation, "
"replacing its previous \"memory resident mode\" (i.e. ``oe-init-build-"
"env-memres``). Now you only need to set :term:`BB_SERVER_TIMEOUT` to a "
"timeout (in seconds) and BitBake's server stays resident for that amount "
"of time between invocations. The ``oe-init-build-env-memres`` script has "
"been removed since a separate environment setup script is no longer "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:27
#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:14
msgid ""
"This section provides information about packaging changes that have "
"occurred:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:30
msgid "``python3`` Changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:32
msgid ""
"The main \"python3\" package now brings in all of the standard Python 3 "
"distribution rather than a subset. This behavior matches what is expected"
" based on traditional Linux distributions. If you wish to install a "
"subset of Python 3, specify ``python-core`` plus one or more of the "
"individual packages that are still produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:38
msgid ""
"``python3``: The ``bz2.py``, ``lzma.py``, and ``_compression.py`` scripts"
" have been moved from the ``python3-misc`` package to the "
"``python3-compression`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:42
msgid ""
"``binutils``: The ``libbfd`` library is now packaged in a separate "
"\"libbfd\" package. This packaging saves space when certain tools (e.g. "
"``perf``) are installed. In such cases, the tools only need ``libbfd`` "
"rather than all the packages in ``binutils``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:47
msgid "``util-linux`` Changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:49
msgid ""
"The ``su`` program is now packaged in a separate \"util-linux-su\" "
"package, which is only built when \"pam\" is listed in the "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` variable. ``util-linux`` should not be installed "
"unless it is needed because ``su`` is normally provided through the "
"shadow file format. The main ``util-linux`` package has runtime "
"dependencies (i.e. :term:`RDEPENDS`) on the ``util-linux-su`` package "
"when \"pam\" is in :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:58
msgid ""
"The ``switch_root`` program is now packaged in a separate \"util-linux-"
"switch-root\" package for small :term:`Initramfs` images that do not need"
" the whole ``util-linux`` package or the busybox binary, which are both "
"much larger than ``switch_root``. The main ``util-linux`` package has a "
"recommended runtime dependency (i.e. :term:`RRECOMMENDS`) on the ``util-"
"linux-switch-root`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:66
msgid ""
"The ``ionice`` program is now packaged in a separate \"util-linux-"
"ionice\" package. The main ``util-linux`` package has a recommended "
"runtime dependency (i.e. :term:`RRECOMMENDS`) on the ``util-linux-"
"ionice`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:71
msgid ""
"``initscripts``: The ``sushell`` program is now packaged in a separate "
"\"initscripts-sushell\" package. This packaging change allows systems to "
"pull ``sushell`` in when ``selinux`` is enabled. The change also "
"eliminates needing to pull in the entire ``initscripts`` package. The "
"main ``initscripts`` package has a runtime dependency (i.e. "
":term:`RDEPENDS`) on the ``sushell`` package when \"selinux\" is in "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:79
msgid ""
"``glib-2.0``: The ``glib-2.0`` package now has a recommended runtime "
"dependency (i.e. :term:`RRECOMMENDS`) on the ``shared-mime-info`` "
"package, since large portions of GIO are not useful without the MIME "
"database. You can remove the dependency by using the "
":term:`BAD_RECOMMENDATIONS` variable if ``shared-mime-info`` is too large"
" and is not required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:86
msgid ""
"*Go Standard Runtime:* The Go standard runtime has been split out from "
"the main ``go`` recipe into a separate ``go-runtime`` recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:94
msgid "``acpitests``: This recipe is not maintained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:96
msgid "``autogen-native``: No longer required by Grub, oe-core, or meta-oe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:99
msgid ""
"``bdwgc``: Nothing in OpenEmbedded-Core requires this recipe. It has "
"moved to meta-oe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:102
msgid ""
"``byacc``: This recipe was only needed by rpm 5.x and has moved to meta-"
"oe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:105
msgid "``gcc (5.4)``: The 5.4 series dropped the recipe in favor of 6.3 / 7.2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:108
msgid "``gnome-common``: Deprecated upstream and no longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:110
msgid ""
"``go-bootstrap-native``: Go 1.9 does its own bootstrapping so this recipe"
" has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:113
msgid ""
"``guile``: This recipe was only needed by ``autogen-native`` and "
"``remake``. The recipe is no longer needed by either of these programs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:117
msgid ""
"``libclass-isa-perl``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB 4, no "
"longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:120
msgid ""
"``libdumpvalue-perl``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB 4, no "
"longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:123
msgid ""
"``libenv-perl``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB 4, no longer "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:126
msgid ""
"``libfile-checktree-perl``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB 4, "
"no longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:129
msgid ""
"``libi18n-collate-perl``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB 4, no"
" longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:132
msgid ""
"``libiconv``: This recipe was only needed for ``uclibc``, which was "
"removed in the previous release. ``glibc`` and ``musl`` have their own "
"implementations. ``meta-mingw`` still needs ``libiconv``, so it has been "
"moved to ``meta-mingw``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:137
msgid ""
"``libpng12``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB. The current "
"``libpng`` is 1.6.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:140
msgid ""
"``libpod-plainer-perl``: This recipe was previously needed for LSB 4, no "
"longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.4.rst:143
msgid ""
"``linux-yocto (4.1)``: This recipe was removed in favor of 4.4, 4.9, 4.10"
" and 4.12."
msgstr ""

