msgid "Python and Python 3 Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:152
msgid "Here are auto-packaging changes to Python and Python 3:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:154
msgid ""
"The script-managed ``python-*-manifest.inc`` files that were previously "
"used to generate Python and Python 3 packages have been replaced with a "
"JSON-based file that is easier to read and maintain. A new task is "
"available for maintainers of the Python recipes to update the JSON file "
"when upgrading to new Python versions. You can now edit the file directly"
" instead of having to edit a script and run it to update the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:162
msgid ""
"One particular change to note is that the Python recipes no longer have "
"build-time provides for their packages. This assumes ``python-foo`` is "
"one of the packages provided by the Python recipe. You can no longer run "
"``bitbake python-foo`` or have a :term:`DEPENDS` on ``python-foo``, but "
"doing either of the following causes the package to work as expected::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:172
msgid "or ::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:176
msgid ""
"The earlier build-time provides behavior was a quirk of the way the "
"Python manifest file was created. For more information on this change "
"please see :yocto_git:`this commit "
"</poky/commit/?id=8d94b9db221d1def42f091b991903faa2d1651ce>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:186
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-kernel` class supports building packages for "
"multiple kernels. If your kernel recipe or ``.bbappend`` file mentions "
"packaging at all, you should replace references to the kernel in package "
"names with ``${KERNEL_PACKAGE_NAME}``. For example, if you disable "
"automatic installation of the kernel image using ``RDEPENDS_kernel-base ="
" \"\"`` you can avoid warnings using "
"``RDEPENDS_${KERNEL_PACKAGE_NAME}-base = \"\"`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:194
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-buildhistory` class commits changes to the "
"repository by default so you no longer need to set ``BUILDHISTORY_COMMIT "
"= \"1\"``. If you want to disable commits you need to set "
"``BUILDHISTORY_COMMIT = \"0\"`` in your configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:199
msgid ""
"The ``beaglebone`` reference machine has been renamed to ``beaglebone-"
"yocto``. The ``beaglebone-yocto`` BSP is a reference implementation using"
" only mainline components available in OpenEmbedded-Core and ``meta-"
"yocto-bsp``, whereas Texas Instruments maintains a full-featured BSP in "
"the ``meta-ti`` layer. This rename avoids the previous name clash that "
"existed between the two BSPs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:206
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-update-alternatives` class no longer works with "
"SysV ``init`` scripts because this usage has been problematic. Also, the "
"``sysklogd`` recipe no longer uses ``update-alternatives`` because it is "
"incompatible with other implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.5.rst:211
msgid ""
"By default, the :ref:`ref-classes-cmake` class uses ``ninja`` instead of "
"``make`` for building. This improves build performance. If a recipe is "
"broken with ``ninja``, then the recipe can set ``OECMAKE_GENERATOR = "
"\"Unix Makefiles\"`` to change back to ``make``."
msgstr ""

