"\"xorgproto\" repository. Thus, the corresponding recipes have also been "
"combined into a single ``xorgproto`` recipe. Any recipes that depend upon"
" the older ``*proto`` recipes need to be changed to depend on the newer "
"``xorgproto`` recipe instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:114
msgid ""
"For names of recipes removed because of this repository change, see the "
":ref:`migration-guides/migration-2.6:removed recipes` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:120
msgid ""
"``distutils`` and ``distutils3`` Now Prevent Fetching Dependencies During"
" the ``do_configure`` Task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:122
msgid ""
"Previously, it was possible for Python recipes that inherited the "
"``distutils`` and ``distutils3`` classes to fetch code during the :ref"
":`ref-tasks-configure` task to satisfy dependencies mentioned in "
"``setup.py`` if those dependencies were not provided in the sysroot (i.e."
" recipes providing the dependencies were missing from :term:`DEPENDS`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:131
msgid ""
"This change affects classes beyond just the two mentioned (i.e. "
"``distutils`` and ``distutils3``). Any recipe that inherits "
"``distutils*`` classes are affected. For example, the ``setuptools`` and "
":ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` recipes are affected since they inherit "
"the ``distutils*`` classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:136
msgid ""
"Fetching these types of dependencies that are not provided in the sysroot"
" negatively affects the ability to reproduce builds. This type of "
"fetching is now explicitly disabled. Consequently, any missing "
"dependencies in Python recipes that use these classes now result in an "
"error during the :ref:`ref-tasks-configure` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:145
msgid "``linux-yocto`` Configuration Audit Issues Now Correctly Reported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:147
msgid ""
"Due to a bug, the kernel configuration audit functionality was not "
"writing out any resulting warnings during the build. This issue is now "
"corrected. You might notice these warnings now if you have a custom "
"kernel configuration with a ``linux-yocto`` style kernel recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:155
msgid "Image/Kernel Artifact Naming Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:157
msgid "The following changes have been made:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:159
msgid ""
"Name variables (e.g. :term:`IMAGE_NAME`) use a new "
":term:`IMAGE_VERSION_SUFFIX` variable instead of :term:`DATETIME`. Using "
":term:`IMAGE_VERSION_SUFFIX` allows easier and more direct changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:164
msgid ""
"The :term:`IMAGE_VERSION_SUFFIX` variable is set in the ``bitbake.conf`` "
"configuration file as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:169
msgid "Several variables have changed names for consistency::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:179
msgid ""
"The ``MODULE_IMAGE_BASE_NAME`` variable has been removed. The module "
"tarball name is now controlled directly with the "
":term:`MODULE_TARBALL_NAME` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:183
msgid ""
"The :term:`KERNEL_DTB_NAME` and :term:`KERNEL_DTB_LINK_NAME` variables "
"have been introduced to control kernel Device Tree Binary (DTB) artifact "
"names instead of mangling ``KERNEL_IMAGE_*`` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:188
msgid ""
"The :term:`KERNEL_FIT_NAME` and :term:`KERNEL_FIT_LINK_NAME` variables "
"have been introduced to specify the name of flattened image tree (FIT) "
"kernel images similar to other deployed artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:193
msgid ""
"The :term:`MODULE_TARBALL_NAME` and :term:`MODULE_TARBALL_LINK_NAME` "
"variable values no longer include the \"module-\" prefix or \".tgz\" "
"suffix. These parts are now hardcoded so that the values are consistent "
"with other artifact naming variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:199
msgid ""
"Added the :term:`INITRAMFS_LINK_NAME` variable so that the symlink can be"
" controlled similarly to other artifact types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:203
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":term:`INITRAMFS_NAME` now uses "
"\"${PKGE}-${PKGV}-${PKGR}-${MACHINE}${IMAGE_VERSION_SUFFIX}\" instead of "
"\"${PV}-${PR}-${MACHINE}-${DATETIME}\", which makes it consistent with "
"other variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:211
msgid "``SERIAL_CONSOLE`` Deprecated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:213
msgid ""
"The ``SERIAL_CONSOLE`` variable has been functionally replaced by the "
":term:`SERIAL_CONSOLES` variable for some time. With the Yocto Project "
"2.6 release, ``SERIAL_CONSOLE`` has been officially deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:217
msgid ""
"``SERIAL_CONSOLE`` will continue to work as before for the 2.6 release. "
"However, for the sake of future compatibility, it is recommended that you"
" replace all instances of ``SERIAL_CONSOLE`` with "
":term:`SERIAL_CONSOLES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:223
msgid ""
"The only difference in usage is that :term:`SERIAL_CONSOLES` expects "
"entries to be separated using semicolons as compared to "
"``SERIAL_CONSOLE``, which expects spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:230
msgid "Configure Script Reports Unknown Options as Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:232
msgid ""
"If the configure script reports an unknown option, this now triggers a QA"
" error instead of a warning. Any recipes that previously got away with "
"specifying such unknown options now need to be fixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:239
msgid "Override Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:241
msgid "The following changes have occurred:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:243
msgid ""
"The ``virtclass-native`` and ``virtclass-nativesdk`` Overrides Have Been "
"Removed: The ``virtclass-native`` and ``virtclass-nativesdk`` overrides "
"have been deprecated since 2012 in favor of ``class-native`` and ``class-"
"nativesdk``, respectively. Both ``virtclass-native`` and ``virtclass-"
"nativesdk`` are now dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:251
msgid "The ``virtclass-multilib-`` overrides for multilib are still valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:253
msgid ""
"The ``forcevariable`` Override Now Has a Higher Priority Than ``libc`` "
"Overrides: The ``forcevariable`` override is documented to be the highest"
" priority override. However, due to a long-standing quirk of how "
":term:`OVERRIDES` is set, the ``libc`` overrides (e.g. ``libc-glibc``, "
"``libc-musl``, and so forth) erroneously had a higher priority. This "
"issue is now corrected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:260
msgid ""
"It is likely this change will not cause any problems. However, it is "
"possible with some unusual configurations that you might see a change in "
"behavior if you were relying on the previous behavior. Be sure to check "
"how you use ``forcevariable`` and ``libc-*`` overrides in your custom "
"layers and configuration files to ensure they make sense."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:266
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The ``build-${BUILD_OS}`` Override Has Been Removed: The "
"``build-${BUILD_OS}``, which is typically ``build-linux``, override has "
"been removed because building on a host operating system other than a "
"recent version of Linux is neither supported nor recommended. Dropping "
"the override avoids giving the impression that other host operating "
"systems might be supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:273
msgid ""
"The \"_remove\" operator now preserves whitespace. Consequently, when "
"specifying list items to remove, be aware that leading and trailing "
"whitespace resulting from the removal is retained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:277
msgid ""
"See the \":ref:`bitbake-user-manual/bitbake-user-manual-metadata:removal "
"(override style syntax)`\" section in the BitBake User Manual for a "
"detailed example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:283
msgid "``systemd`` Configuration is Now Split Into ``systemd-conf``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:285
msgid ""
"The configuration for the ``systemd`` recipe has been moved into a "
"``systemd-conf`` recipe. Moving this configuration to a separate recipe "
"avoids the ``systemd`` recipe from becoming machine-specific for cases "
"where machine-specific configurations need to be applied (e.g. for "
"``qemu*`` machines)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:291
msgid "Currently, the new recipe packages the following files::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:300
msgid ""
"If you previously used bbappend files to append the ``systemd`` recipe to"
" change any of the listed files, you must do so for the ``systemd-conf`` "
"recipe instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:307
msgid "Automatic Testing Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:309
msgid "This section provides information about automatic testing changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:311
msgid ""
"``TEST_IMAGE`` Variable Removed: Prior to this release, you set the "
"``TEST_IMAGE`` variable to \"1\" to enable automatic testing for "
"successfully built images. The ``TEST_IMAGE`` variable no longer exists "
"and has been replaced by the :term:`TESTIMAGE_AUTO` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:317
msgid ""
"Inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-testimage` and :ref:`ref-classes-"
"testsdk` classes: best practices now dictate that you use the "
":term:`IMAGE_CLASSES` variable rather than the :term:`INHERIT` variable "
"when you inherit the :ref:`ref-classes-testimage` and :ref:`ref-classes-"
"testsdk` classes used for automatic testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:326
msgid "OpenSSL Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:328
msgid ""
"`OpenSSL <https://www.openssl.org/>`__ has been upgraded from 1.0 to 1.1."
" By default, this upgrade could cause problems for recipes that have both"
" versions in their dependency chains. The problem is that both versions "
"cannot be installed together at build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:335
msgid "It is possible to have both versions of the library at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:342
msgid ""
"The server logfile ``bitbake-cookerdaemon.log`` is now always placed in "
"the :term:`Build Directory` instead of the current directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:348
msgid "Security Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:350
msgid ""
"The Poky distribution now uses security compiler flags by default. "
"Inclusion of these flags could cause new failures due to stricter "
"checking for various potential security issues in code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:357
msgid "Post Installation Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:359
msgid ""
"You must explicitly mark post installs to defer to the target. If you "
"want to explicitly defer a postinstall to first boot on the target rather"
" than at root filesystem creation time, use ``pkg_postinst_ontarget()`` "
"or call ``postinst_intercept delay_to_first_boot`` from "
"``pkg_postinst()``. Any failure of a ``pkg_postinst()`` script (including"
" exit 1) triggers an error during the :ref:`ref-tasks-rootfs` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:366
msgid ""
"For more information on post-installation behavior, see the \":ref:`dev-"
"manual/new-recipe:post-installation scripts`\" section in the Yocto "
"Project Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:373
msgid "Python 3 Profile-Guided Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:375
msgid ""
"The ``python3`` recipe now enables profile-guided optimization. Using "
"this optimization requires a little extra build time in exchange for "
"improved performance on the target at runtime. Additionally, the "
"optimization is only enabled if the current :term:`MACHINE` has support "
"for user-mode emulation in QEMU (i.e. \"qemu-usermode\" is in "
":term:`MACHINE_FEATURES`, which it is by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:384
msgid ""
"If you wish to disable Python profile-guided optimization regardless of "
"the value of :term:`MACHINE_FEATURES`, then ensure that "
":term:`PACKAGECONFIG` for the ``python3`` recipe does not contain "
"\"pgo\". You could accomplish the latter using the following at the "
"configuration level::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:392
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can set :term:`PACKAGECONFIG` using an append file for"
" the ``python3`` recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.6.rst:400
