msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:88
msgid ""
"``bind``: The ``nsupdate`` binary has been moved to the ``bind-utils`` "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:91
msgid ""
"Debug split: The default debug split has been changed to create separate "
"source packages (i.e. ``package_name-dbg`` and ``package_name-src``). If "
"you are currently using ``dbg-pkgs`` in :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` to bring "
"in debug symbols and you still need the sources, you must now also add "
"``src-pkgs`` to :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES`. Source packages remain in the "
"target portion of the SDK by default, unless you have set your own value "
"for :term:`SDKIMAGE_FEATURES` that does not include ``src-pkgs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:101
msgid ""
"Mount all using ``util-linux``: ``/etc/default/mountall`` has moved into "
"the -mount sub-package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:104
msgid ""
"Splitting binaries using ``util-linux``: ``util-linux`` now splits each "
"binary into its own package for fine-grained control. The main ``util-"
"linux`` package pulls in the individual binary packages using the "
":term:`RRECOMMENDS` and :term:`RDEPENDS` variables. As a result, existing"
" images should not see any changes assuming :term:`NO_RECOMMENDATIONS` is"
" not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:112
msgid ""
"``netbase/base-files``: ``/etc/hosts`` has moved from ``netbase`` to "
"``base-files``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:115
msgid ""
"``tzdata``: The main package has been converted to an empty meta package "
"that pulls in all ``tzdata`` packages by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:118
msgid ""
"``lrzsz``: This package has been removed from ``packagegroup-self-"
"hosted`` and ``packagegroup-core-tools-testapps``. The X/Y/ZModem support"
" is less likely to be needed on modern systems. If you are relying on "
"these packagegroups to include the ``lrzsz`` package in your image, you "
"now need to explicitly add the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-2.7.rst:132
msgid "*gcc*: Drop version 7.3 recipes. Version 8.3 now remains."
