#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:95
msgid "``python-scons``: Removed the Python 2.x version of the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:97
msgid "``source-highlight``: No longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:99
msgid "``stress``: Replaced by ``stress-ng``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:101
msgid ""
"``vulkan``: Split into ``vulkan-loader``, ``vulkan-headers``, and "
"``vulkan-tools``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:104
msgid "``weston-conf``: Functionality moved to ``weston-init``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:111
msgid "The following packaging changes have occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:113
msgid ""
"The :wikipedia:`Epiphany <GNOME_Web>` browser has been dropped from "
"``packagegroup-self-hosted`` as it has not been needed inside ``build-"
"appliance-image`` for quite some time and was causing resource problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:118
msgid ""
"``libcap-ng`` Python support has been moved to a separate ``libcap-ng-"
"python`` recipe to streamline the build process when the Python bindings "
"are not needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:122
msgid ""
"``libdrm`` now packages the file ``amdgpu.ids`` into a separate ``libdrm-"
"amdgpu`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:125
msgid ""
"``python3``: The ``runpy`` module is now in the ``python3-core`` package "
"as it is required to support the common \"python3 -m\" command usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:129
msgid ""
"``distcc`` now provides separate ``distcc-client`` and ``distcc-server`` "
"packages as typically one or the other are needed, rather than both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:133
msgid ""
"``python*-setuptools`` recipes now separately package the "
"``pkg_resources`` module in a ``python-pkg-resources`` / ``python3-pkg-"
"resources`` package as the module is useful independent of the rest of "
"the setuptools package. The main ``python-setuptools`` / "
"``python3-setuptools`` package depends on this new package so you should "
"only need to update dependencies unless you want to take advantage of the"
" increased granularity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:144
msgid "CVE Checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:146
msgid ""
"``cve-check-tool`` has been functionally replaced by a new ``cve-update-"
"db`` recipe and functionality built into the ``cve-check`` class. The "
"result uses NVD JSON data feeds rather than the deprecated XML feeds that"
" ``cve-check-tool`` was using, supports CVSSv3 scoring, and makes other "
"improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:152
msgid ""
"Additionally, the ``CVE_CHECK_CVE_WHITELIST`` variable has been replaced "
"by ``CVE_CHECK_WHITELIST`` (replaced by :term:`CVE_CHECK_IGNORE` in "
"version 4.0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:160
msgid "The following BitBake changes have occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:162
msgid ""
"``addtask`` statements now properly validate dependent tasks. Previously,"
" an invalid task was silently ignored. With this change, the invalid task"
" generates a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:166
msgid ""
"Other invalid ``addtask`` and ``deltask`` usages now trigger these "
"warnings: \"multiple target tasks arguments with addtask / deltask\", and"
" \"multiple before/after clauses\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:170
msgid ""
"The \"multiconfig\" prefix is now shortened to \"mc\". \"multiconfig\" "
"will continue to work, however it may be removed in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:173
msgid ""
"The ``bitbake -g`` command no longer generates a ``recipe-depends.dot`` "
"file as the contents (i.e. a reprocessed version of ``task-depends.dot``)"
" were confusing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:177
msgid ""
"The ``bb.build.FuncFailed`` exception, previously raised by "
"``bb.build.exec_func()`` when certain other exceptions have occurred, has"
" been removed. The real underlying exceptions will be raised instead. If "
"you have calls to ``bb.build.exec_func()`` in custom classes or "
"``tinfoil-using`` scripts, any references to ``bb.build.FuncFailed`` "
"should be cleaned up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:184
msgid ""
"Additionally, the ``bb.build.exec_func()`` no longer accepts the "
"\"pythonexception\" parameter. The function now always raises exceptions."
" Remove this argument in any calls to ``bb.build.exec_func()`` in custom "
"classes or scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:189
msgid ""
"The ``BB_SETSCENE_VERIFY_FUNCTION2`` variable is no longer used. In the "
"unlikely event that you have any references to it, they should be "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:193
msgid ""
"The ``RunQueueExecuteScenequeue`` and ``RunQueueExecuteTasks`` events "
"have been removed since setscene tasks are now executed as part of the "
"normal runqueue. Any event handling code in custom classes or scripts "
"that handles these two events need to be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:198
msgid ""
"The arguments passed to functions used with :term:`BB_HASHCHECK_FUNCTION`"
" have changed. If you are using your own custom hash check function, see "
":yocto_git:`/poky/commit/?id=40a5e193c4ba45c928fccd899415ea56b5417725` "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:204
msgid ""
"Task specifications in ``BB_TASKDEPDATA`` and class implementations used "
"in signature generator classes now use \"<fn>:<task>\" everywhere rather "
"than the \".\" delimiter that was being used in some places. This change "
"makes it consistent with all areas in the code. Custom signature "
"generator classes and code that reads ``BB_TASKDEPDATA`` need to be "
"updated to use ':' as a separator rather than '.'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:214
msgid "Sanity Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:216
msgid "The following sanity check changes occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:218
msgid ":term:`SRC_URI` is now checked for usage of two problematic items:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:221
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\"${PN}\" prefix/suffix use --- warnings always appear if ${PN} is used. "
"You must fix the issue regardless of whether multiconfig or anything else"
" that would cause prefixing/suffixing to happen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:225
msgid ""
"Github archive tarballs --- these are not guaranteed to be stable. "
"Consequently, it is likely that the tarballs will be refreshed and thus "
"the :term:`SRC_URI` checksums will fail to apply. It is recommended that "
"you fetch either an official release tarball or a specific revision from "
"the actual Git repository instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:231
msgid ""
"Either one of these items now trigger a warning by default. If you wish "
"to disable this check, remove ``src-uri-bad`` from :term:`WARN_QA`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:235
msgid ""
"The ``file-rdeps`` runtime dependency check no longer expands "
":term:`RDEPENDS` recursively as there is no mechanism to ensure they can "
"be fully computed, and thus races sometimes result in errors either "
"showing up or not. Thus, you might now see errors for missing runtime "
"dependencies that were previously satisfied recursively. Here is an "
"example: package A contains a shell script starting with ``#!/bin/bash`` "
"but has no dependency on bash. However, package A depends on package B, "
"which does depend on bash. You need to add the missing dependency or "
"dependencies to resolve the warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:245
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Setting ``DEPENDS_${PN}`` anywhere (i.e. typically in a recipe) now "
"triggers an error. The error is triggered because :term:`DEPENDS` is not "
"a package-specific variable unlike RDEPENDS. You should set "
":term:`DEPENDS` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:250
msgid ""
"systemd currently does not work well with the musl C library because only"
" upstream officially supports linking the library with glibc. Thus, a "
"warning is shown when building systemd in conjunction with musl."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:260
msgid "The following miscellaneous changes have occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:262
msgid ""
"The ``gnome`` class has been removed because it now does very little. You"
" should update recipes that previously inherited this class to do the "
"following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:268
msgid ""
"The ``meta/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-dtb.inc`` file has been removed. "
"This file was previously deprecated in favor of setting "
":term:`KERNEL_DEVICETREE` in any kernel recipe and only produced a "
"warning. Remove any ``include`` or ``require`` statements pointing to "
"this file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:274
msgid ""
":term:`TARGET_CFLAGS`, :term:`TARGET_CPPFLAGS`, :term:`TARGET_CXXFLAGS`, "
"and :term:`TARGET_LDFLAGS` are no longer exported to the external "
"environment. This change did not require any changes to core recipes, "
"which is a good indicator that no changes will be required. However, if "
"for some reason the software being built by one of your recipes is "
"expecting these variables to be set, then building the recipe will fail. "
"In such cases, you must either export the variable or variables in the "
"recipe or change the scripts so that exporting is not necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:286
msgid ""
"You must change the host distro identifier used in "
":term:`NATIVELSBSTRING` to use all lowercase characters even if it does "
"not contain a version number. This change is necessary only if you are "
"not using :ref:`ref-classes-uninative` and :term:`SANITY_TESTED_DISTROS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:292
msgid ""
"In the ``base-files`` recipe, writing the hostname into ``/etc/hosts`` "
"and ``/etc/hostname`` is now done within the main :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"install` function rather than in the ``do_install_basefilesissue`` "
"function. The reason for the change is because "
"``do_install_basefilesissue`` is more easily overridden without having to"
" duplicate the hostname functionality. If you have done the latter (e.g. "
"in a ``base-files`` bbappend), then you should remove it from your "
"customized ``do_install_basefilesissue`` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:302
msgid ""
"The ``wic --expand`` command now uses commas to separate \"key:value\" "
"pairs rather than hyphens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:307
msgid "The wic command-line help is not updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:309
msgid ""
"You must update any scripts or commands where you use ``wic --expand`` "
"with multiple \"key:value\" pairs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:312
msgid ""
"UEFI image variable settings have been moved from various places to a "
"central ``conf/image-uefi.conf``. This change should not influence any "
"existing configuration as the ``meta/conf/image-uefi.conf`` in the core "
"metadata sets defaults that can be overridden in the same manner as "
"before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-3.0.rst:318
msgid ""
"``conf/distro/include/world-broken.inc`` has been removed. For cases "
"where certain recipes need to be disabled when using the musl C library, "
"these recipes now have ``COMPATIBLE_HOST_libc-musl`` set with a comment "
"that explains why."
msgstr ""

