#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:133
msgid "ipk packaging changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:135
msgid ""
"ipk packaging (using ``opkg``) now uses ``zstd`` compression instead of "
"``xz`` for better compression and performance. This does mean that "
"``.ipk`` packages built using the 5.0 release requires Opkg built with "
"zstd enabled --- naturally this is the case in 5.0, but at least by "
"default these packages will not be usable on older systems where Opkg "
"does not have zstd enabled at build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:141
msgid ""
"Additionally, the internal dependency solver in Opkg is now deprecated "
"--- it is still available in this release but will trigger a warning if "
"selected. The default has been the external ``libsolv`` solver for some "
"time, but if you have explicitly removed that from :term:`PACKAGECONFIG` "
"for Opkg to select the internal solver, you should plan to switch to "
"``libsolv`` in the near future (by including ``libsolv`` your custom "
":term:`PACKAGECONFIG` value for Opkg, or reverting to the default value)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:151
msgid "motd message when using ``DISTRO = \"poky\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:153
msgid ""
"The default ``poky`` :term:`DISTRO` is explicitly a *reference* "
"distribution for testing and development purposes.  It enables most "
"hardware and software features so that they can be tested, but this also "
"means that from a security point of view the attack surface is very "
"large."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:158
msgid ""
"We encourage anyone using the Yocto Project for production use to create "
"their own distribution and not use Poky. To encourage this behaviour "
"further, in 5.0 a warning has been added to ``/etc/motd`` when Poky is "
"used so that the developer will see it when they log in. If you are "
"creating your own distribution this message will not show up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/migration-5.0.rst:164
msgid ""
"For information on how to create your own distribution, see \":ref:`dev-"
"manual/custom-distribution:creating your own distribution`\"."
