#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:6
msgid ""
"This is a Long Term Support release, published in April 2022, and "
"supported at least for two years (April 2024)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:9
msgid "New Features / Enhancements in 4.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:11
msgid "Linux kernel 5.15, glibc 2.35 and ~300 other recipe upgrades"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:13
msgid ""
"Reproducibility: this release fixes the reproducibility issues with "
"``rust-llvm`` and ``golang``. Recipes in OpenEmbedded-Core are now fully "
"reproducible. Functionality previously in the optional \"reproducible\" "
"class has been merged into the :ref:`ref-classes-base` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:18
msgid ""
"Network access is now disabled by default for tasks other than where it "
"is expected to ensure build integrity (where host kernel supports it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:20
msgid ""
"The Yocto Project now allows you to reuse the Shared State cache from its"
" autobuilder. If the network connection between our server and your "
"machine is faster than you would build recipes from source, you can try "
"to speed up your builds by using such Shared State and Hash Equivalence "
"by setting::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:31
msgid ""
"The Python package build process is now based on `wheels "
"<https://pythonwheels.com/>`__ in line with the upstream direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:34
msgid ""
"New :ref:`ref-classes-overlayfs` and :ref:`ref-classes-overlayfs-etc` "
"classes and ``overlayroot`` support in the :term:`Initramfs` framework to"
" make it easier to overlay read-only filesystems (for example) with "
":wikipedia:`OverlayFS <OverlayFS>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-4.0.rst:39
msgid ""
"Inclusive language adjustments to some variable names - see the :ref:`4.0"
" migration guide <migration-4.0-inclusive-language>` for details."
