"``matchbox-terminal``: add ``x-terminal-emulator`` as :term:`RPROVIDES` "
"and set :term:`ALTERNATIVE` for the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:618
msgid ""
"``default-providers.conf``: set ``rxvt-unicode`` as the default "
"``virtual-x-terminal-emulator`` runtime provider with "
":term:`PREFERRED_RPROVIDER`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:622
msgid ""
"``cve-update-nvd2-native``: updating the database will now result in an "
"error if :term:`BB_NO_NETWORK` is enabled and ``CVE_DB_UPDATE_INTERVAL`` "
"is not set to ``-1``. Users can control the NVD database source using the"
" ``NVD_DB_VERSION`` variable with possible values ``NVD1``, ``NVD2``, or "
"``FKIE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:628
msgid ""
"``systemtap``: add ``--with-extra-version=\"oe\"`` configure option to "
"improve the reproducibility of the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:631
msgid ""
"``python3``: package ``tkinter``'s shared objects separately in the "
"``python3-tkinter`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:634
msgid ""
"``init-manager``: set the variable ``VIRTUAL-RUNTIME_dev_manager`` to "
"``udev`` by default in :oe_git:`meta/conf/distro/include/init-manager-"
"none.inc </openembedded-core/tree/meta/conf/distro/include/init-manager-"
"none.inc>` and :oe_git:`meta/conf/distro/include/init-manager-"
"sysvinit.inc </openembedded-core/tree/meta/conf/distro/include/init-"
"manager-sysvinit.inc>`, instead of :oe_git:`meta/recipes-"
"core/packagegroups/packagegroup-core-boot.bb </openembedded-"
"core/tree/meta/recipes-core/packagegroups/packagegroup-core-boot.bb>` "
"only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:644
msgid ""
"Likewise, the same is done for ``VIRTUAL-RUNTIME_keymaps`` with "
"``keymaps`` as its default value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:647
msgid ""
"``seatd``: Create a ``seat`` group and package the systemd service "
"``seatd.service`` with correct permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:650
msgid ""
"That way, the ``weston`` user in ``weston-init.bb`` was added to the "
"``seat`` group to be able to properly establish connection between the "
"Weston and the ``seatd`` socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:654
msgid "``webkitgtk``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:656
msgid "Fix build on 32bit arches with 64bit ``time_t`` only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:658
msgid "Disable JIT on RISCV64."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:660
msgid ":ref:`ref-classes-report-error`: Add :term:`PN` to error report files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:662
msgid "``initrdscripts``: add UBI support for mounting a live ``ubifs`` rootfs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:664
msgid "``uboot-extlinux-config.bbclass``: add support for device tree overlays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:666
msgid "``glibc``: add ``ld.so.conf`` to :term:`CONFFILES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:668
msgid ""
"``udev-extraconf``: Allow FAT mount group to be specified with "
":term:`MOUNT_GROUP`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:671
msgid ""
"New ``bbverbnote`` log utility which can be used to print on the console "
"(equivalent to the ``bb.verbnote`` Python implementation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:674
msgid ""
":ref:`ref-classes-grub-efi`: Add :term:`GRUB_TITLE` variable to set "
"custom GRUB titles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:677
msgid ""
"``gawk``: Enable high precision arithmetic support by default (``mpfr`` "
"enabled by default in :term:`PACKAGECONFIG`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:680
msgid ""
"``licenses``: Map the license ``SGIv1`` to ``SGI-OpenGL``, as ``SGIv1`` "
"is not an SPDX license identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:683
msgid ""
"Configuration files for the `b4 <https://b4.docs.kernel.org>`__ command-"
"line tool was added to the different Yocto Project and OpenEmbedded "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:687
msgid ""
"``kernel-fitimage``: handle :doc:`multiconfig </dev-manual/multiconfig>` "
"dependency when :term:`INITRAMFS_MULTICONFIG` is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:691
msgid ""
"``psplash``: when using the ``systemd`` feature from "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`, start the ``psplash`` service when the "
"``/dev/fb0`` framebuffer is detected with Udev."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:695
msgid "``gdb``: is now compiled with xz support by default (``--with-lzma``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:697
msgid ""
"``busybox``: drop net-tools from the default ``defconfig``, since these "
"tools (``ifconfig``, etc.) have been deprecated since `2009 "
"<https://lists.debian.org/debian-devel/2009/03/msg00780.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:701
msgid "``perf`` is built with ``zstd`` in :term:`PACKAGECONFIG` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:703
msgid "``boost``: add ``charconv`` to built libraries by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:705
msgid ""
"``mirrors``: rationalise Debian mirrors to point at the canonical server "
"(deb.debian.org) instead of country specific ones. This server is backed "
"by a :wikipedia:`CDN <Content_delivery_network>` to properly balance the "
"server load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:710
msgid ""
"``lib: sbom30``: Add action statement for affected VEX statements with "
"\"Mitigation action unknown\", as these are not tracked by the existing "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:715
#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:993
#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:763
#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.1.rst:734
msgid "Known Issues in |yocto-ver|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:717
msgid ""
"The ``cve-check`` class is based on the `National Vulnerability Database "
"<https://nvd.nist.gov/>`__ (NVD). Since the beginning of 2024, the "
"maintainers of this database have stopped annotating CVEs with the "
"affected CPEs. This prevents the ``cve-check`` class to properly report "
"CVEs as CPEs are used to match Yocto recipes with CVEs affecting them. As"
" a result, the current CVE reports may look good but the reality is that "
"some vulnerabilities are just not reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:725
msgid ""
"During that time, users may look up the 'CVE database "
"<https://www.cve.org/>'__ for entries concerning software they use, or "
"follow release notes of such projects closely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.2.rst:729
msgid ""
"Please note, that the ``cve-check`` tool has always been a helper tool, "
"and users are advised to always review the final result. Results of an "
"automatic scan may not take into account configuration options, compiler "
"options and other factors."
msgstr ""

