#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:109
msgid ""
"``tinfoil``: add a ``wait_for`` decorator to wrap a function that makes "
"an asynchronous tinfoil call wait for event to say that the call has been"
" successful, or an error has occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:113
msgid ""
"New ``bb.utils.to_filemode()`` helper function which is a helper to take "
"a variable's content containing a filemode and convert it to the proper "
"Python representation of the number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:117
msgid ""
"``cooker``: Use a shared counter for processing parser jobs. This allows "
"the parser processes to run independently of needing to be feed by the "
"parent process, and load balances them much better."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:121
msgid ""
"``cooker/process/utils``: Add a ``-P`` (``--profile``) option to "
":term:`BitBake` to specify what to profile. Can be \"main\", \"idle\" or "
"\"parsing\". Split the reports in separate files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:125
msgid ""
"A \"filtering\" functionality was added and allows modifying the value of"
" a variable before its value is returned by :term:`BitBake`. The "
"``setVarFilter`` API can be used for applying the filters, but it is "
"**not** recommended for general use. It was added for internal use in the"
" :term:`OpenEmbedded Build System` in the :ref:`ref-classes-native` "
"class. The list of filters that are allowed are derived from a select "
"list of functions that must be added using a ``filter_proc`` decorator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:133
msgid ""
"``tests/parse``: Add tests for ``include``, ``require`` and "
"``include_all``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:136
msgid "Toolchain changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:138
msgid "The Clang/LLVM toolchain can now be used as part of the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:140
msgid ""
"The :term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_TARGET`, "
":term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_NATIVE` and :term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_SDK` "
"variables can be used to customize the selected toolchain globally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:144
msgid ""
"There are two supported toolchains: \"gcc\" and \"clang\". See the "
"documentation of :term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_TARGET` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:147
msgid ""
"The toolchain is also customizable on a per-recipe basis, using the "
":term:`TOOLCHAIN` and :term:`TOOLCHAIN_NATIVE` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:152
msgid ""
"The :term:`TOOLCHAIN` should **not** be set globally. For overriding the "
"toolchain globally, use :term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_TARGET`, "
":term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_NATIVE` and :term:`PREFERRED_TOOLCHAIN_SDK`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-5.3.rst:156
msgid ""
"Multiple recipes were pinned to use the GCC/Binutils toolchain as they do"
" not support being built with Clang/LLVM yet. In these recipes the "
":term:`TOOLCHAIN` variable is set to \"gcc\"."
msgstr ""

