msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:57
msgid ""
"``libconfig``: Import recipe from :oe_git:`/meta-openembedded/`, needed "
"by one of the Mesa recipes "
"(:oecore_rev:`1a0196a794f8858c4715871558e97c3d69deb19e`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:60
msgid ""
"``python3-sphinxcontrib-svg2pdfconverter``: Used for the generation of "
"the Yocto Project documentation "
"(:oecore_rev:`f3f001967744b593fb39c32058d29595bbf0ffb6`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:63
msgid ""
"``python3-pyzstd``: Import from :oe_git:`meta-python </meta-"
"openembedded/tree/meta-python>`, needed by the ``ukify`` tool of systemd "
"v258 (:oecore_rev:`88a27133c184125e1503d1397cbd276a9a76f6ab`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:67
msgid ""
"``python3-uv-build``: This recipe adds the ``uv`` Python build backend, "
"required by ``python3-cryptography`` "
"(:oecore_rev:`0880cd2b79ee47274d62035e354aa4b93966b4d0`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:70
msgid ""
"``blueprint-compiler``: Add the recipe as it became a dependency of the "
"``epiphany`` recipe after its upgrade to 49.2 "
"(:oecore_rev:`4212392ca7ebf890e1e192ddd0e7dbe1f8dabcf2`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:73
msgid ""
"``python3-sbom-cve-check``: New recipe for building and using `sbom-cve-"
"check <https://github.com/bootlin/sbom-cve-check>`__, a lightweight SBOM "
"CVE analysis tool "
"(:oecore_rev:`0fdacec2d7101d3fe638b430c43b1e14acd148ae`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:78
msgid ""
"``python3-shacl2code``, ``python3-hatch-build-scripts``, ``python3-spdx-"
"python-model``: Added as dependencies of ``python3-sbom-cve-check`` "
"(:oecore_rev:`48622216cb1a80f9cc127ebb08e13cc455d09240`, "
":oecore_rev:`41591afd51ddbdaf1779799f4258a81afcff238d`, "
":oecore_rev:`a83eaca5d9f3e2eb76a5d3c6bb42cf3b3bfe92fb`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:85
msgid ""
"``libfyaml``: Added as a dependency of ``appstream`` "
"(:oecore_rev:`b8b7b5873fecef4040c5f35d5a0e857f8f9fc907`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:88
msgid ""
"``meta-world-recipe-sbom``: Building this recipe will produce SBOM "
"documents for each recipe present in the build environment, using the "
":ref:`ref-classes-create-spdx` class. This is different from the image "
"SBOM which can also be generated using the :ref:`ref-classes-create-spdx`"
" class after building an image. See :doc:`/dev-manual/sbom` for more "
"information (:oecore_rev:`d999ac407c86b462134008818d5863ecb577f3c6`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:96
msgid ""
"``python3-kirk``: The Kirk application is a fork of ``runltp-ng`` and "
"became the official `LTP <https://linux-test-"
"project.readthedocs.io/en/latest/>`__ tests executor "
"(:oecore_rev:`c33fd4e50a66ace990f3820f980876bfbfc07baa`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:101
msgid ""
"``wic``: This recipe builds the :doc:`WIC </dev-manual/wic>` command-line"
" tool. This used to be part of :term:`OpenEmbedded-Core (OE-Core)` but is"
" now externally managed "
"(:oecore_rev:`25ca1cb46dd6d0c57f61f2dc3b649601dc81b50c`, "
":oecore_rev:`b9e2a2f584376076c4552bef7309c81b9fe986c0`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:109
msgid ""
":ref:`ref-classes-kernel-yocto-rust`: Adds the required dependencies to "
"build the Rust components of the Linux kernel "
"(:oecore_rev:`6c90097bebeffe7c5be35fc56e61b1994f03d6a9`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:113
msgid ""
":ref:`ref-classes-module-rust`: Support for building out-of-tree Rust "
"kernel modules. An example recipe using this class can be found in "
":oecore_path:`meta-skeleton/recipes-kernel/rust-out-of-tree-module` "
"(:oecore_rev:`76fd22f09fab6c1de339dac310f9b31cb5e4ad69`, "
":oecore_rev:`76fd22f09fab6c1de339dac310f9b31cb5e4ad69`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:119
msgid ""
":ref:`ref-classes-sbom-cve-check`: Class for post-build CVE analysis of "
"an image, which uses the `sbom-cve-check <github.com/bootlin/sbom-cve-"
"check>`__ tool internally "
"(:oecore_rev:`8ef22ad9e302f86b2da4fa81541a464e95b9ef3c`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:124
msgid ""
":ref:`ref-classes-sbom-cve-check-recipe`: Class for post-build CVE "
"analysis of recipes (using the recipe SBOM, meaning building the software"
" provided by the recipe is not needed), which uses the `sbom-cve-check "
"<github.com/bootlin/sbom-cve-check>`__ tool internally. This also "
"obsoletes the ``cve-check`` class. "
"(:oecore_rev:`e2518b1eaabef13c9f8d44b52b8ec9d4dd4ed916`, "
":oecore_rev:`00de455f8d3aeca880129d23e8cfb7e246404699`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:134
msgid ""
"The :term:`OPENSSH_HOST_KEY_DIR` variable can be used to specify the "
"directory where OpenSSH host keys are stored. The default value is "
"``/etc/ssh`` (:oecore_rev:`addd80ddfd892eb4513f323d369d210935416e05`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:138
msgid ""
"The :term:`OPENSSH_HOST_KEY_DIR_READONLY_CONFIG` variable can be used to "
"specify the directory where OpenSSH host keys are stored when the device "
"uses a read-only filesystem. The default value is ``/var/run/ssh`` "
"(:oecore_rev:`addd80ddfd892eb4513f323d369d210935416e05`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:143
msgid ""
"The :term:`SPDX_INCLUDE_KERNEL_CONFIG` can be set to \"1\" to export the "
"Linux kernel configuration (``CONFIG_*`` parameters) into the SPDX "
"document when using the :ref:`ref-classes-create-spdx` class "
"(:oecore_rev:`228a968e7c47d811c06143279bdb0f9c5f374bef`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:148
msgid ""
"The :term:`SPDX_INCLUDE_PACKAGECONFIG` variable can be set to \"1\" to "
"export a recipe's :term:`PACKAGECONFIG` features (enabled/disabled) into "
"the SPDX document when using the :ref:`ref-classes-create-spdx` class "
"(:oecore_rev:`228a968e7c47d811c06143279bdb0f9c5f374bef`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:153
msgid ""
"The :term:`SPDX_PACKAGE_URL` allows specifying a space-separated list of "
"Package URLs (purls) for the software Package when using the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-create-spdx` class "
"(:oecore_rev:`874b2d301d3cac617b1028bc6ce91b1f916a6508`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:158
msgid ""
"The :term:`SPDX_GIT_PURL_MAPPINGS` variable allows mapping domain names "
"to PURLs (Package URLs) in SPDX documents "
"(:oecore_rev:`9f1825e74d0f70917676201286b148aea84cc660`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../migration-guides/release-notes-6.0.rst:162
